WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:01.240
(audience clapping)
- Welcome back y'all.

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.130
It's Christmas and across America

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:04.510
there are countless charities

00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:07.550
working hard to provide holiday
magic for those in need.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.565
We've even met a number of them this week,

00:00:09.565 --> 00:00:12.340
well my next guests are
part of that generosity.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.040
But instead of giving toys or food

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.320
they do something different,
they provide Christmas trees.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.210
For many people it's the
most important gift of all.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.830
Let's welcome David and Michelle.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.460
Y'all give it up!
(audience claps and cheers)

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.150
So thank you so much
for being on the show,

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:28.983
I'm very excited to have you here.

00:00:28.983 --> 00:00:31.757
But Michelle this all started,
was it from a Craigslist ad?

00:00:31.757 --> 00:00:32.590
Was it?
- It was yeah.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.780
We live in Colorado Springs and I have--

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:35.900
- Yeah love yeah.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.130
- Beautiful there.
- Yeah beautiful.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.900
- I have three kids, five grandchildren.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.497
And I wanted a new Christmas
tree for that year.

00:00:42.497 --> 00:00:45.740
So we went off to the store,
came home with a new tree,

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:48.036
and I was like "what are we
gonna do with our old tree?"

00:00:48.036 --> 00:00:51.710
And so we decided to put it on Craigslist.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:56.040
And within about an
hour we got 20 responses

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.166
that they would want our tree.

00:00:58.166 --> 00:00:58.999
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:00:58.999 --> 00:00:59.860
- We had one.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.580
And so we were pretty

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:07.050
moved and we really wanted
to give all 20 a tree,

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.060
but we only had one.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:11.670
And so that's kind of
snowballed into this project

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.950
11 years later.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.980
- What a beautiful way that it started.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.100
(audience clapping) You
know you were simply

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.570
just trying to be like
hey anybody need a tree?

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.305
And then you found out there
was such a need for it.

00:01:19.305 --> 00:01:23.380
So what struck you David
about these requests?

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.380
- Well it was a couple of things.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:26.070
One was the number, how quickly they came,

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.740
but I think what really touched
me they told us the stories.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:29.610
I mean it was a single mom

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:30.801
and she told us why she was struggling.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:33.980
It was a wounded vet, a
single dad raising three kids

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:34.930
and he just wanted a tree.

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:37.110
There was a boys home and
they told us some stories

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:37.943
about the boys home.

00:01:37.943 --> 00:01:40.650
So many times we get tears of gratitude.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:41.483
- [Kelly] I imagine.

00:01:41.483 --> 00:01:42.950
- 'Cause one of the
things that we didn't get

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.150
before this whole thing happened

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:47.080
was how deeply meaningful
a Christmas tree is

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.920
and how painful it is,
especially as a parent,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.300
if you can't give your kids a tree.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.660
Probably one of the more
meaningful requests we got

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:57.890
it was from a little girl,
she was 10-years-old,

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.920
and she had a brain
injury when she was young

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.080
and she was going blind.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.330
And so right?

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.220
And so it was a family
that had a bunch of kids

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.080
and they were kind of struggling

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:06.500
to deal with their medical
bills and everything else

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:07.333
and there was no way

00:02:07.333 --> 00:02:08.166
they could afford a tree.
- I imagine.

00:02:08.166 --> 00:02:08.999
- Right?
- Wow.

00:02:08.999 --> 00:02:10.737
- So she said to her mom,

00:02:10.737 --> 00:02:13.547
"mommy we must have a tree this year,

00:02:13.547 --> 00:02:15.686
"it's the last one I'll ever see."

00:02:15.686 --> 00:02:16.519
- That makes me--
- Right?

00:02:16.519 --> 00:02:17.352
- Cry every time

00:02:17.352 --> 00:02:18.185
I hear the story.
- I mean,

00:02:18.185 --> 00:02:19.018
I'm gonna need a minute.

00:02:19.018 --> 00:02:20.440
- Right right right.
- I mean what?

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.600
Oh my gosh.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.160
So since that first Christmas
how many trees have you given?

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.500
- Over 4,000 trees.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.333
- [Kelly] What?

00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:29.420
- Yeah (audience claps) all
across the United States.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.253
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:30.253 --> 00:02:31.870
- And all around the world.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:32.860
- Wow.
- And it's not

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:33.970
just trees though.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:37.070
In my family we had a tradition
of what went on a tree.

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:41.670
And so we also provide
ornaments, tinsel, candy cane,

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.870
lights.
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.150
- [Michelle] Everything to put together

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:46.210
a really beautiful tree for their home.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.709
- Oh my gosh it's so great.

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:49.720
(audience claps) And to like have family,

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.050
like my kids would love
to be able to do this

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.460
for other kids you know what I'm saying?

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.780
To even get like at
home like with your kids

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.110
to be like oh what can I do to like--

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.850
- I got 100 names in LA.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:02:59.683
- Do you?

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.192
Don't you challenge me sir.

00:03:02.192 --> 00:03:03.822
(everyone laughs)

00:03:03.822 --> 00:03:04.655
I will--
- 100.

00:03:04.655 --> 00:03:05.710
100--
- I am not kidding.

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:07.010
Like I want that list.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:09.640
And I will, I literally,
I think every year

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.120
like 'cause my kids are very blessed,

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.600
I didn't grow up with like anything.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.170
And my kids are so blessed.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.040
And so it's one of those things

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.140
I think it's really important

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.227
no matter what household you grow up in

00:03:17.227 --> 00:03:20.860
to always know to take
care of your neighbors

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:21.840
and your friends,
(audience claps)

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.613
and other people, specially
when you're so blessed.

00:03:25.613 --> 00:03:26.446
- Okay.

00:03:26.446 --> 00:03:28.260
- So what a fun thing to do like you know

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:30.290
for any mom out there or dad out there

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:31.900
looking to be like let's
do something with our kids

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.630
like as a family to help another family.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.450
It's a beautiful thing.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.283
Okay.

00:03:36.283 --> 00:03:38.930
David and Michelle
clearly embody the message

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.210
that it's far better
to give than to receive

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:44.070
so in that spirit I
wanna give them something

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.770
other than the fact that I want that list

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.330
'cause I wanna help those people.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:49.690
But on behalf of our show

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:51.952
we'd like to give your
charity 10,000 dollars.

00:03:51.952 --> 00:03:54.817
(audience cheering)

00:03:54.817 --> 00:03:55.841
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:55.841 --> 00:03:56.674
- [David] Thank you.

00:03:56.674 --> 00:03:58.418
- I think that sounds like so much fun

00:03:58.418 --> 00:04:00.268
to be able to help people.

00:04:00.268 --> 00:04:02.518
It's a beautiful thing.
- Thank you so much.

